# Polish pass

- Stack: Next.js 15 App Router (do not downgrade), TypeScript, Tailwind. Server components by default, "use client" only where interactivity needs it.
- Never change, move or restyle these live routes or their data/state: /champions-draft, /rugby-draft, /pub-quiz, /games/longest-word, /draft, /wardrobe-ai, and anything under them. If you edit a shared component, check every file that imports it.
- /hire easter eggs (hire-meter finale card, Rudi modal, FELINE_DISTRACTION_DETECTED card) are intentional. Never remove or alter them.
- Contact forms stay on Formspree. Don't change action, method or field names.
- Don't weaken Supabase RLS. No secrets or service keys in client code.
- Design: base #0A0A0F, amber #F59E0B as the only strong accent. DM Serif Display for headings, Geist for body, Geist Mono for labels. No new fonts or colour tokens. Opacity tints of existing colours are fine.
- No new npm dependencies unless the task explicitly allows one.
- Copy: no em dashes or en dashes, use plain hyphens. No filler. Banned: passionate, journey, seamless, leverage, crafting digital experiences, "I'd love to", "reaching out", synergy. Plain, dry NI English.
- Never invent metrics, client results, user counts or testimonials. Keep client status labels exactly as currently written. ShelterLink must not be described as in use by Assisi. RV's online ordering/payments must not be claimed.
- All animation respects prefers-reduced-motion.
- After every task: npm run build and npm run lint pass, then commit with a clear message.
